vigate to the Rocketchat web at http://the-agent-company.com:3000/home.\\n     3\\t\\n     4\\t* Use the provided april-attendance-data.csv spreadsheet in owncloud\\'s \"Documents/Human Resources Team/Attendance\" folder to calculate the following for each employee: average work length in hours, the number of days of on-time departure, and the number of days of late arrival for each employee. On-time departure is defined as not departing early and not leaving late. Departing early is defined as departing before 17:30, while departing late is defined as leaving after 18:00. Late arrival is defined as arriving later than 9:00.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t* Through RocketChat, you need to ask Chen Xinyi about who are in the finance or technical department, ask David Wong about who are in the HR or sales/marketing department, and ask Mark Johnson about who are in the product/UX or documentation department.\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t* Create a report called \"department-april-attendace.xlsx\" in the local /workspace directory. You must make sure that it is a xlsx file.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t* In the report, have columns with names \\'Name\\', \\'Department Average Work Length\\', \\'Departmetn Average On-time Departure Count\\', and \\'Department Average Late Arrival Count\\'. Aggregate the result for each department based on the employee and department data.\\n', path='/instruction/task.md', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'ownCloud'}, thought='Now I understand the task. I need to:\\n1. Access OwnCloud and download the attendance data\\n2. Access RocketChat to get department information from specific people\\n3. Calculate metrics from the attendance data\\n4. Create an Excel report with department-level aggregates\\n\\nLet me first check if there are existing SOPs for these platforms before proceeding.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservati